Configuration complète pour l'Intermediate CA
1. Créer la clé privée de l'Intermediate CA :
bash

Collapse


 Copy

openssl genrsa -out intermediate-ca-key.pem 4096
2. Créer le fichier de configuration pour la CSR (intermediate-ca-csr.conf) :
bash

Collapse


 Copy

cat > intermediate-ca-csr.conf << EOF
[req]
distinguished_name = req_distinguished_name
req_extensions = v3_req
prompt = no

[req_distinguished_name]
C = FR
ST = France
L = Paris
O = Gouvernement
OU = IT Department - Dev Division
CN = dev.dg01.kubo.rie.go.ff Intermediate CA

[v3_req]
basicConstraints = CA:TRUE
keyUsage = keyCertSign, cRLSign
EOF
3. Créer la Certificate Signing Request (CSR) :
bash

Collapse


 Copy

openssl req -new -key intermediate-ca-key.pem -out intermediate-ca.csr -config intermediate-ca-csr.conf
4. Créer le fichier de configuration pour la signature (intermediate-ca-signing.conf) :
bash

Collapse


 Copy

cat > intermediate-ca-signing.conf << EOF
[v3_intermediate_ca]
basicConstraints = critical,CA:TRUE,pathlen:0
keyUsage = critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign
subjectKeyIdentifier = hash
authorityKeyIdentifier = keyid:always,issuer:always
nameConstraints = critical,@name_constraints
crlDistributionPoints = @crl_section
authorityInfoAccess = @ocsp_section

[name_constraints]
permitted;DNS.1 = dev.dg01.kubo.rie.go.ff
permitted;DNS.2 = .dev.dg01.kubo.rie.go.ff

[crl_section]
URI.1 = http://crl.kubo.rie.go.ff/intermediate.crl

[ocsp_section]
caIssuers;URI.1 = http://certs.kubo.rie.go.ff/intermediate.crt
OCSP;URI.1 = http://ocsp.kubo.rie.go.ff
EOF
5. Signer l'Intermediate CA avec la Root CA :
bash

Collapse


 Copy

openssl x509 -req -in intermediate-ca.csr \
    -CA root-ca-cert.pem \
    -CAkey root-ca-key.pem \
    -CAcreateserial \
    -out intermediate-ca-cert.pem \
    -days 1825 \
    -sha256 \
    -extensions v3_intermediate_ca \
    -extfile intermediate-ca-signing.conf
6. Créer la chaîne de certificats complète :
bash

